  "security_implications": "This chunk handles response integrity generation via tlul_rsp_intg_gen (parameters EnableRspIntgGen/EnableDataIntgGen) and command integrity checking via tlul_cmd_intg_chk when CmdIntgCheck is true. The response fields d_data, d_opcode, d_error are protected by response integrity. intg_error carries command integrity violations; if unused or disconnected, tampered commands could be processed silently. Parameter UserInIsZero=1 forces user data to zero, preventing information leaks. Disabling integrity generation via parameters would completely bypass integrity protection, enabling data tampering.",
